#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0554-D expect=noViolation domain=AE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when, in an Associated Persons dataset (DOMAIN starting with AP), APID is not present.
#note "The split discriminator against the sibling CDISC-CG0554-C, and the ONLY production-reachable scenario on this rule: a non-AP dataset (DOMAIN=AE, class EVENTS) carrying STUDYID and AESEQ but none of USUBJID/APID/SPDEVID/POOLID - which is exactly CDISC-CG0554-C's violation data - is SILENT here, because the AP half's prefix(DOMAIN, 2) =~ AP conjunct is false. The missing subject identifier is the sibling's finding alone. Recovered from the retired CORE-000107, whose third fixture this was; deleting it left nothing pinning that -D stays quiet on -C's data."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 1 | Headache
S1 | AE | 2 | Nausea
---
